Now let's understand tasks:

1. **"Drag to look still unuseable. Fix that."** — Mouse drag look on desktop (when pointer lock not available?) Currently click on canvas requests pointer lock. But "drag to look" suggests desktop drag look should work — currently only pointer lock mousemove works. Also mobile look zone only covers a small element. Need to implement robust drag-to-look: pointerdown on canvas → drag; also pointer lock. Let's implement pointer-based drag with pointer events on canvas, plus pointer lock optional toggle. The main issue: after start, canvas.requestPointerLock. If pointer lock fails or user drags, no effect. Also maybe pointer lock got engaged but movementX works. "Drag to look still unuseable" — likely mouse drag doesn't rotate because only pointerLocked mousemove. Let's add: pointerdown on canvas, pointermove while dragging, since pointer lock might not be granted in iframe. Also allow pointer lock but fallback. Add sensitivity and pitch clamps wider (-0.55 to 0.95). Also touch drag anywhere outside controls. Add full-screen look layer? Better: attach pointer events on canvas. Let's implement:

```js
let dragging=false,dragPointer=null,lastX=0,lastY=0;
canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown',e=>{ if(!isStarted||pointerLocked) return; dragging=true;dragPointer=e.pointerId;lastX=e.clientX;lastY=e.clientY;canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); });
canvas.addEventListener('pointermove',e=>{ if(dragging&&e.pointerId===dragPointer){ yaw-=(e.clientX-lastX)*.0042; pitch=clamp(pitch+(e.clientY-lastY)*.0032,-.5,.95); lastX=...; }});
canvas.addEventListener('pointerup',...);
```
But canvas click also requests pointer lock. If we request pointer lock on pointerup when not dragged much. Could be annoying: in iframe pointer lock may fail. Let's request pointer lock on click still; pointer lock movement then works. Actually if pointer lock succeeds, drag pointer doesn't matter. If pointer lock is blocked silently (promise rejection), drag fallback works. But pointer lock request might throw? It returns promise. Fine.

Also perhaps allow drag on desktop always even when pointer locked? No.

Mobile `look-zone`: currently a small area "DRAG TO LOOK". Better make whole non-control screen drag area. Add a full-screen `.look-zone` overlay positioned absolute inset with pointer-events none? Then touchstart on document. Simpler: attach touch handlers to canvas and a full-screen overlay behind controls. Existing `#look-zone` is inside touch-controls. Let's inspect CSS for touch-controls/look-zone. Grep.

