content.text:
I introduced a typo in oldString? It matched, but the old function I supplied contains `rig.arms[0].rotation.x+=(Math.sin...` etc; fine. Need check actual for broken text like `head.y` etc; I used proper above. Let me later run node --check.

Important: In `animateHumans` dialogue branch, `e.activityClock` increments. Good.

Need also update `e.x/e.z` when patrol; done. But when not moving, e.x stays last. Fine.

`chooseNpcTarget` uses `collidesAt` which includes gate wing walls etc.

Now camera fix. Replace updateCamera room transparency. Also need no material modifications. Implement wall-specific camera clamp.

`collidesAt` signature currently `(x,z,r)`, add optional `kind` param? For camera indoors we need only wall colliders. Modify:

```js
function collidesAt(x,z,r=PLAYER_RADIUS,kind=null){for(const c of colliders){if(c.open)continue;if(kind&&c.kind!==kind)continue;...}}
```
Then camera use `collidesAt(cx,cz,.18,'wall')`.

But NPCs/cats use default all. Good.

Implement updateCamera:
```js
function updateCamera(dt){
 const room=interiorAt(...);
 if(window.__freezeCamera)return;
 const target=...
 if(room){
   const dist=4.6;
   const h=Math.cos(pitch)*dist, v=Math.sin(pitch)*dist;
   const desired=...
   desired.x=clamp(...);desired.z=clamp(...);desired.y=clamp(desired.y,1.2,room.h-.55);
   let safe=1; for i sample walls ... if collidesAt(...,'wall') safe...
   const clipped = target.lerp(desired,safe);
   camera.position.lerp(clipped,...); camera.lookAt(...)
   return
 }
 ...
}
```
But target at player y+1.45, sample y ignored for walls but fine. If player near wall and camera direction outward, safe small -> camera close. Could allow camera to move upward for overhead. Also target should be inside.

Better indoor camera: fixed over-shoulder height 2.9 and distance 3.4. Rooms 16-18 deep; okay. We can keep 4.6. The exterior camera still 7.8.

Also hide ceiling/roof? Not necessary. But interior ceiling joists etc y5; camera y target 1.45+1.1+sin(.24)*4.6≈4.6? Could be near ceiling 5.4. Set indoor distance 3.8 and vertical 1.0 to avoid clipping roof. `v = Math.sin(pitch)*3.8` with pitch .24 → .9; y≈3.5. fine.

Let's patch collidesAt and updateCamera.

