content.text:
Now input rewrite. Replace section from `// ----- Input and camera -----` through touch look listeners. Keep touch movement/buttons. Need implement robust drag.

Current code:
```js
const keys={};let yaw=0,pitch=.24,run=false,pointerLocked=false;
document.addEventListener('keydown',...)
...
canvas.addEventListener('click',()=>{...requestPointerLock})
document.addEventListener('pointerlockchange',...)
document.addEventListener('mousemove',...)
function isMobile...
if(isMobile())...
let touchLook=null;
$('#look-zone').addEventListener('touchstart'...)
...
```
Replace mousemove/drag section.

Plan:
- Add `const shell=$('#game-shell');` maybe later `$` already defined at line ~? Yes `$` defined before input (line ~1100). Use.
- Keydown: init audio on any key? Call audio.init() on keydown once. Add KeyK mute toggle, maybe KeyM still. `if(e.code==='KeyK'){...}`.
- Canvas click: request pointer lock only if not drag. Instead use `pointerup` logic.
- Pointer drag on shell with target exclusions.
- Keep pointer lock mousemove.
- Remove old `#look-zone` touch handlers, or keep? Remove to avoid double. Add a visual hint? The element still exists but pointer-events none; no listeners. Fine.

Implementation:

```js
const keys={};let yaw=0,pitch=.24,run=false,pointerLocked=false;
let lookDrag=null,lastPointerTap=0;
function initAudioOnce(){audio.init();}
document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{ audio.init(); ...});
...
const shell=$('#game-shell');
const noLookTarget=target=>target.closest('button, a, input, .modal-screen, .dialogue-card, .map-panel, .mission-card, .location-card, .topbar, .touch-controls button');
shell.addEventListener('pointerdown',e=>{
  if(!isStarted||dialogueOpen)return;
  if(e.pointerType==='mouse'&&e.button!==0)return;
  if(noLookTarget(e.target))return;
  audio.init();
  if(pointerLocked)return;
  lookDrag={id:e.pointerId,x:e.clientX,y:e.clientY,moved:0,type:e.pointerType};
  try{shell.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId)}catch{}
});
shell.addEventListener('pointermove',e=>{
  if(pointerLocked)return;
  if(!lookDrag||e.pointerId!==lookDrag.id)return;
  const dx=e.clientX-lookDrag.x,dy=e.clientY-lookDrag.y;
  lookDrag.x=e.clientX;lookDrag.y=e.clientY;lookDrag.moved+=Math.abs(dx)+Math.abs(dy);
  const s=e.pointerType==='touch'?1.35:1;
  yaw-=dx*.0042*s;
  pitch=THREE.MathUtils.clamp(pitch+dy*.0030*s,-.5,1.02);
  if(e.cancelable)e.preventDefault();
});
const endLook=e=>{
  if(!lookDrag||e.pointerId!==lookDrag.id)return;
  const wasTap=lookDrag.moved<6;const type=lookDrag.type;
  lookDrag=null;
  if(wasTap&&type==='mouse'&&!isMobile()&&isStarted&&!dialogueOpen&&$('#puzzle-screen').classList.contains('hidden')&&$('#help-screen').classList.contains('hidden')&&$('#start-screen').classList.contains('hidden'))canvas.requestPointerLock?.();
};
shell.addEventListener('pointerup',endLook);
shell.addEventListener('pointercancel',e=>{if(lookDrag&&e.pointerId===lookDrag.id)lookDrag=null});
document.addEventListener('pointer$...`? Canvas is inside shell; pointerup target may be canvas, bubbles to shell. Good.
```

But pointer capture on shell means pointermove targeted to shell. good.

Potential pointer lock request on every click even on HUD? Excluded by target check; but topbar excluded. Fine.

Issue pointer lock in iframe may throw promise rejection; no error. In Chrome may require user gesture; pointerup is gesture. Fine. But when pointer lock is active, clicking toggles? canvas click handler requests lock again. Harmless.

Add `document.addEventListener('pointerlockerror',...)` no need.

`mousemove` while pointer locked: `yaw-=movementX*.0024; pitch=clamp(...,-.5,1.02)`. Good.

Touch: pointerdown on shell with touch works but the on-screen D-pad buttons excluded by `.touch-controls button`. The `.look-zone` is pointer-events none. The D-pad background `div` is not a button and could trigger look; but only button taps matter. Fine.

Need `e.preventDefault()` on pointerdown? To prevent text selection; shell CSS `touch-action:none` on canvas only. Add `#game-shell{touch-action:none}`? CSS. Could add `document.body` touch-action none? Already overflow hidden. Add `#game-shell{touch-action:none}` to style. Let's do.

Also `lookDrag` handles drag while pointerLocked false. When pointer lock active, pointerdown ignored, but mousemove via document. Good.

Also start screen: clicking BEGIN calls audio init, requestPointerLock. Good.

Keyboard: call audio.init.

