content.text:
Now, checkpoint and spireDoor groups: static but they contain sprite labels; sprites skipped. But checkpoint sphere and boxes merge away from group; entity references group only for position/labels. That's fine. But wait — merging removes meshes from group; labels remain. Fine.

However, there's an issue: `station` groups dynamic, and their labels are children too, skipped anyway.

Dynamic check: traverse up to world; `world` itself not dynamic.

Now write batch function. Add before `localLights` computation near line ~2200. Also call it before localLights. Order matters: localLights built from scene traversal; lights unaffected.

Implementation:

```js
// ----- Static batching -----
const BATCH_CELL=26;
function batchStaticWorld(){
  world.updateMatrixWorld(true);
  const buckets=new Map();
  const candidates=[];
  world.traverse(o=>{
    if(!o.isMesh||o.isInstancedMesh||o.isSkinnedMesh)return;
    if(o.userData.dynamic)return;
    let p=o.parent;
    while(p&&p!==world){if(p.userData.dynamic)return;p=p.parent}
    const mat=o.material;
    if(!mat||Array.isArray(mat)||mat.transparent)return;
    const geo=o.geometry;
    if(!geo||!geo.attributes.position)return;
    if(o.userData.noBatch)return;
    const wp=new THREE.Vector3().setFromMatrixPosition(o.matrixWorld);
    const cx=Math.floor(wp.x/BATCH_CELL),cz=Math.floor(wp.z/BATCH_CELL);
    const attrs=Object.keys(geo.attributes).sort().join(',');
    const key=mat.uuid+'|'+cx+'|'+cz+'|'+(o.castShadow?1:0)+'|'+(geo.index?1:0)+'|'+attrs;
    let b=buckets.get(key);
    if(!b){b={mat,cast:o.castShadow,geos:[]};buckets.set(key,b)}
    b.geos.push(o);
  });
  let mergedCount=0,removed=0;
  for(const b of buckets.values()){
    if(b.geos.length<2)continue;
    const geos=[];
    for(const m of b.geos){const g=m.geometry.clone();g.applyMatrix4(m.matrixWorld);geos.push(g)}
    const merged=mergeGeometries(geos,false);
    geos.forEach(g=>g.dispose());
    if(!merged)continue;
    const mesh=new THREE.Mesh(merged,b.mat);
    mesh.castShadow=b.cast;mesh.receiveShadow=true;
    mesh.matrixAutoUpdate=false;
    mesh.computeBoundingSphere?.();
    world.add(mesh);
    for(const m of b.geos){m.parent.remove(m)} // geometry shared primitives, don't dispose
    mergedCount++;removed+=b.geos.length;
  }
  return {mergedCount,removed};
}
```

Careful: cloned geometry of shared boxGeo with matrixWorld includes world transform. world has identity transform, so merged mesh in world at origin is correct. But if world ever transformed, no. Fine.

`matrixAutoUpdate=false` with identity matrix (default) fine.

`mesh.frustumCulled=true` default.

Potential issue: geometry attributes mismatch due to `uv` presence — key covers.

Potential issue: `mergeGeometries` with morph attributes—none.

Potential issue: Some meshes have `onBeforeRender` or are used later (e.g., reference kept and material changed) — we skipped known dynamic ones. But there might be other runtime references: e.g. `bulb.material.emissiveIntensity` at construction only. `windowMat` instanced. Search for references to specific mesh variables updated in loop. `gateLeft/gateRight.position.x` — perimeter gate meshes! Those are separate meshes added where? Let me check. `gateLeft` and `gateRight` created at perimeter, and updated in updateWorld. Are they children of world directly or a group? If direct world meshes without dynamic flag, merging would break gate animation. Let me find.

Also `paradise` is scene-level. `fogWisps` sprites. `petFx` sprites. `shade` static.

